<?xml version="1.0"?>
<ScenContainer xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema">
  <ScenTitle>Indian Fury 2 - Mozambique Madness, 1994</ScenTitle>
  <ScenDescription>&lt;BODY scroll=auto&gt;&lt;P style="FONT-SIZE: 14px; TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; FONT-VARIANT: normal; WHITE-SPACE: normal; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: rgb(0,0,0); FONT-STYLE: normal; TEXT-ALIGN: left; ORPHANS: 2; LETTER-SPACING: normal; TEXT-INDENT: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px"&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;Indian Fury&amp;nbsp;2 – Mozambique Madness&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14px; CURSOR: text; TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; FONT-VARIANT: normal; WHITE-SPACE: normal; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FLOAT: none; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: rgb(0,0,0); FONT-STYLE: normal; TEXT-ALIGN: left; ORPHANS: 2; DISPLAY: inline !important; LETTER-SPACING: normal; BACKGROUND-COLOR: rgb(255,255,255); TEXT-INDENT: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px"&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;
&lt;P style="FONT-SIZE: 14px; TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; FONT-VARIANT: normal; WHITE-SPACE: normal; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: rgb(0,0,0); FONT-STYLE: normal; TEXT-ALIGN: left; ORPHANS: 2; LETTER-SPACING: normal; TEXT-INDENT: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px"&gt;This is the second scenario of an 8-10 scenario campaign. This scenario is linked to the Northern Fury Campaign and you may wish to refer to that background document to get a broader picture of the geopolitical setting. This scenario happens simultaneously with the first episode set in the Indian Ocean/Persian Gulf area, Persian Pounce. These two scenarios are also concurrent to Northern Fury 1: H Hour, Northern Fury 2: X-Ray Station, Northern Fury 3: Dagger to the Heart, Caribbean Fury 1: Hot Tamale’s and others. It is not essential to play any of these scenarios prior to taking your place as Admiral Commanding the HMS Ark Royal Battle Group. See the Indian Fury background document for further insight on the background and specific issues in this region. The key nuggets are&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14px; CURSOR: text; TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; FONT-VARIANT: normal; WHITE-SPACE: normal; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FLOAT: none; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: rgb(0,0,0); FONT-STYLE: normal; TEXT-ALIGN: left; ORPHANS: 2; DISPLAY: inline !important; LETTER-SPACING: normal; BACKGROUND-COLOR: rgb(255,255,255); TEXT-INDENT: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px"&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;
&lt;UL style="FONT-SIZE: 14px; TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; FONT-VARIANT: normal; WHITE-SPACE: normal; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: rgb(0,0,0); FONT-STYLE: normal; TEXT-ALIGN: left; ORPHANS: 2; LETTER-SPACING: normal; TEXT-INDENT: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px"&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;The Cold War continued no, thaw in relations. Germany is reunified but causing friction between East &amp;amp; West. WP still alive and doing very well.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Yesterday, 12 Feb 1994, the Winter Olympics in Lillehammer, opened with ominous indications of trouble brewing. Soviet and Eastern Bloc countries were represented at the opening ceremonies but many of their athletes were not present at the start of the actual events this morning. The Russian Olympic village was empty and initial investigation found that many of the athletes had simply disappeared, while only a few had flown home. Norway ordered the IOC to cancel the games and evacuate the Olympic Village.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Norway has called up its reserves, deployed forces to forward bases and has requested support from NATO. The request for support was submitted to the North Atlantic Council (NAC) 4 hours ago.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;About 40 minutes ago (1300Hrs Zulu (Greenwich Mean Time) on 13 Feb 1994) you received news that hostilities in Europe had commenced and that there were attacks in North America. So far things in this area are quiet.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;It is 1645hrs local, 1345Z and you are enjoying the end of a pleasant day at sea with minimal air operations on the flight deck. What could possibly go wrong?&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14px; CURSOR: text; TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; FONT-VARIANT: normal; WHITE-SPACE: normal; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FLOAT: none; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: rgb(0,0,0); FONT-STYLE: normal; TEXT-ALIGN: left; ORPHANS: 2; DISPLAY: inline !important; LETTER-SPACING: normal; BACKGROUND-COLOR: rgb(255,255,255); TEXT-INDENT: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px"&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;
&lt;P style="FONT-SIZE: 14px; TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; FONT-VARIANT: normal; WHITE-SPACE: normal; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: rgb(0,0,0); FONT-STYLE: normal; TEXT-ALIGN: left; ORPHANS: 2; LETTER-SPACING: normal; TEXT-INDENT: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px"&gt;Your Battle Group has just completed a long scheduled port visit to Cape Town South Africa, which was more of a diplomatic mission to welcome the post-Apartheid nation back into the fold of the western world. Your force is not ready for operations at the moment, and in fact only three of the six ships under your command are currently in company.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14px; CURSOR: text; TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; FONT-VARIANT: normal; WHITE-SPACE: normal; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FLOAT: none; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: rgb(0,0,0); FONT-STYLE: normal; TEXT-ALIGN: left; ORPHANS: 2; DISPLAY: inline !important; LETTER-SPACING: normal; BACKGROUND-COLOR: rgb(255,255,255); TEXT-INDENT: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px"&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;
&lt;P style="FONT-SIZE: 14px; TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; FONT-VARIANT: normal; WHITE-SPACE: normal; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: rgb(0,0,0); FONT-STYLE: normal; TEXT-ALIGN: left; ORPHANS: 2; LETTER-SPACING: normal; TEXT-INDENT: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px"&gt;As you travel up the Mozambique Channel between Africa and Madagascar, you begin to receive disturbing news from Europe and North America. After conferring with your staff and the Captain of the Ark Royal, you direct them to make contingency plans should you be directed to cut your tour with CTF-150 (Combined Task Force 150 – the international force protecting shipping in the Gulf of Aden and African coast) short and head to either the Persian Gulf or the Mediterranean. At least things should be quiet for the next few days of passage north.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14px; CURSOR: text; TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; FONT-VARIANT: normal; WHITE-SPACE: normal; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FLOAT: none; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: rgb(0,0,0); FONT-STYLE: normal; TEXT-ALIGN: left; ORPHANS: 2; DISPLAY: inline !important; LETTER-SPACING: normal; BACKGROUND-COLOR: rgb(255,255,255); TEXT-INDENT: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px"&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;
&lt;P style="FONT-SIZE: 14px; TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; FONT-VARIANT: normal; WHITE-SPACE: normal; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: rgb(0,0,0); FONT-STYLE: normal; TEXT-ALIGN: left; ORPHANS: 2; LETTER-SPACING: normal; TEXT-INDENT: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px"&gt;For posture and disposition of various Gulf allies please see the background document.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14px; CURSOR: text; TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; FONT-VARIANT: normal; WHITE-SPACE: normal; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FLOAT: none; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: rgb(0,0,0); FONT-STYLE: normal; TEXT-ALIGN: left; ORPHANS: 2; DISPLAY: inline !important; LETTER-SPACING: normal; BACKGROUND-COLOR: rgb(255,255,255); TEXT-INDENT: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px"&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;
&lt;P style="FONT-SIZE: 14px; TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; FONT-VARIANT: normal; WHITE-SPACE: normal; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: rgb(0,0,0); FONT-STYLE: normal; TEXT-ALIGN: left; ORPHANS: 2; LETTER-SPACING: normal; TEXT-INDENT: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px"&gt;------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14px; CURSOR: text; TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; FONT-VARIANT: normal; WHITE-SPACE: normal; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FLOAT: none; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: rgb(0,0,0); FONT-STYLE: normal; TEXT-ALIGN: left; ORPHANS: 2; DISPLAY: inline !important; LETTER-SPACING: normal; BACKGROUND-COLOR: rgb(255,255,255); TEXT-INDENT: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px"&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;
&lt;P style="FONT-SIZE: 14px; TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; FONT-VARIANT: normal; WHITE-SPACE: normal; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: rgb(0,0,0); FONT-STYLE: normal; TEXT-ALIGN: left; ORPHANS: 2; LETTER-SPACING: normal; TEXT-INDENT: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px"&gt;Designer’s notes:&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14px; CURSOR: text; TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; FONT-VARIANT: normal; WHITE-SPACE: normal; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FLOAT: none; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: rgb(0,0,0); FONT-STYLE: normal; TEXT-ALIGN: left; ORPHANS: 2; DISPLAY: inline !important; LETTER-SPACING: normal; BACKGROUND-COLOR: rgb(255,255,255); TEXT-INDENT: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px"&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;
&lt;P style="FONT-SIZE: 14px; TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; FONT-VARIANT: normal; WHITE-SPACE: normal; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: rgb(0,0,0); FONT-STYLE: normal; TEXT-ALIGN: left; ORPHANS: 2; LETTER-SPACING: normal; TEXT-INDENT: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px"&gt;This scenario is somewhat complex, mostly because of the limited resources at your disposal. At times, you will have fights in several distinct areas happening simultaneously and because of the vast areas to be transited you would benefit from using quick-jump keys, missions and Weapons Release Authority (WRA) to manage your forces.&lt;/P&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14px; CURSOR: text; TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; FONT-VARIANT: normal; WHITE-SPACE: normal; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FLOAT: none; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: rgb(0,0,0); FONT-STYLE: normal; TEXT-ALIGN: left; ORPHANS: 2; DISPLAY: inline !important; LETTER-SPACING: normal; BACKGROUND-COLOR: rgb(255,255,255); TEXT-INDENT: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px"&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;
&lt;UL style="FONT-SIZE: 14px; TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; FONT-VARIANT: normal; WHITE-SPACE: normal; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: rgb(0,0,0); FONT-STYLE: normal; TEXT-ALIGN: left; ORPHANS: 2; LETTER-SPACING: normal; TEXT-INDENT: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px"&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;You should turn 'special messages' ON and in a Pop-Up, and scenario events OFF.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Please respect the initial ready times for aircraft, this represents designed delays that both balance the scenario and paint the picture of routine air operations where machinery breaks and requires preventive maintenance inspections and repairs.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;There is a British KC-130 available in Kenya, unlike the US, the Brits and many other nations have C-130s that can work as either Tanker or Cargo, and the loadout options reflect this. I believe that the rapid changing from one configuration to the other however is a significant piece of work (12+hrs plus stowage of equipment) and generally outside the scope of operating at a remote site. Therefore you should leave this KC-130 as a tanker – you will be tempted to change it later in the scenario but the events will not work with it in any case.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Your initial tasks are quite vague; you and your staff are wondering if the war that started in Europe less than an hour ago will spread. You must be careful not to start hostilities yourself – I am sure that with everything going on around the world – another conflict in a remote corner of the world would not be good for your annual report!&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Recommend that you have a word or text document open in the background to allow you to cut and paste the numerous special messages you will receive. This will allow you to refer to them later at your leisure to double check details of tasking or assignments.&lt;/LI&gt;
&lt;LI&gt;Points are allotted or deducted for losses, and for accomplishing assigned tasks.&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/UL&gt;&lt;SPAN style="FONT-SIZE: 14px; CURSOR: text; TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; FONT-VARIANT: normal; WHITE-SPACE: normal; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FLOAT: none; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: rgb(0,0,0); FONT-STYLE: normal; TEXT-ALIGN: left; ORPHANS: 2; DISPLAY: inline !important; LETTER-SPACING: normal; BACKGROUND-COLOR: rgb(255,255,255); TEXT-INDENT: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px"&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;
&lt;P style="FONT-SIZE: 14px; TEXT-DECORATION: none; FONT-FAMILY: Verdana,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; FONT-VARIANT: normal; WHITE-SPACE: normal; WORD-SPACING: 0px; TEXT-TRANSFORM: none; FONT-WEIGHT: 400; COLOR: rgb(0,0,0); FONT-STYLE: normal; TEXT-ALIGN: left; ORPHANS: 2; LETTER-SPACING: normal; TEXT-INDENT: 0px; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px"&gt;Created by Bart Gauvin: AKA Gunner98&lt;/P&gt;&lt;/BODY&gt;</ScenDescription>
